{{~##
   The module's implementation: the per-record reads, the table loads and the accessor's
   storage. Split from the header because a USTRUCT's methods cannot be defined inline in
   a header UHT parses without the definitions landing in every translation unit.

   Reads go straight into the members. The reader has an overload per engine type, so
   there is no temporary to declare and no conversion to apply - the block that used to
   be three lines per field is one.

   Failure is checked once per table rather than once per field. The reader's failure is
   sticky: the first read that runs out of data records why and the rest do nothing. Two
   places do have to look at it mid-flight, and both are loops whose trip count came off
   the wire - a corrupt count would otherwise spin appending default elements until the
   allocator gave up.
##~}}
